<h2 id='key-features' emoji='⚙️'>⚙️ Key Features Head-to-Head</h2>

<h3>Email Automation</h3>

Moosend's visual automation builder supports conditional splits, wait steps, lead scoring actions, and website behavior triggers. You can build a full new-client onboarding sequence that branches based on which service they booked, whether they've opened previous emails, and whether they've visited your pricing page. AWeber's automation is linear by comparison — functional for simple drip sequences, but it struggles with multi-condition logic that modern retention marketing requires.

<StarRating product='AWeber Automation' rating={3.2} />
<StarRating product='Moosend Automation' rating={4.6} />

<h3>List Segmentation</h3>

Moosend lets you segment on virtually any combination of contact data, behavioral signals, and custom fields. For a med spa, this means you can target "clients who had a filler treatment in the last 6 months AND haven't booked a follow-up AND opened at least one email in the last 30 days." AWeber's segmentation is tag-based and simpler — workable for small lists, but as your client database grows, the lack of multi-condition filtering becomes a real bottleneck.

<h3>Templates and Design</h3>

Both platforms offer responsive, professionally designed templates. AWeber has a larger raw template count (700+), but quantity doesn't equal quality. Moosend's template library is smaller but more modern, and the editor renders more predictably across email clients including Gmail on mobile — which matters because that's where a significant portion of your client base reads their inbox.

<h3>Landing Pages and Forms</h3>

Both tools include landing page builders. Moosend's pages load faster (it's measurably leaner on external scripts) and include A/B testing natively. AWeber's landing pages are solid and have improved, but they lack the native A/B testing that conversion-focused operators need for lead generation campaigns around service promotions or new patient offers.

<h3>Analytics and Reporting</h3>

Moosend tracks revenue per email campaign if you connect an e-commerce or booking source — a meaningful feature for med spas running retail (skincare products, gift cards) alongside services. AWeber's reporting covers the standard metrics well but doesn't extend to revenue attribution. For operators who want to tie email activity directly to bookings and revenue, Moosend wins cleanly here.

<h3>Customer Support</h3>

This is AWeber's genuine advantage. Phone support is rare at this price point, and AWeber has maintained it. Moosend offers email and live chat support — fast and knowledgeable in our experience, but there's no phone option. For operators who are less tech-comfortable or managing a team with high turnover, AWeber's phone support has real value.

